<%
// PRJEDU_pages: what a page may see. A page runs with the VISITOR's role,
// and nobody logs in here: role 0, Guest. MNT_CODE's xdb_acl gives Guest
// no rights, so it reads as empty here - while a script of the engine
// itself (role 9, System) reads it fine: start() could log it.
var title = "Access";
var refresh = 0;
var code = evt.GetValue("id('MNT_CODE')/@val");
var lvl = evt.GetValue("id('T1_LVL')/@val");
-%>
<%@ include file="part/head.ayp" %>
<h1>What this page may read</h1>
<table>
  <tr><th>Value</th><th>xdb_acl</th><th>Read by this page</th></tr>
  <tr><td>T1_LVL</td><td>(none: open)</td><td><%= lvl %></td></tr>
  <tr><td>MNT_CODE</td><td>0xFFFFFFF0 (nothing for role 0)</td>
      <td><%= code == null ? "(nothing - not readable for this visitor)" : code %></td></tr>
</table>
<p>Your role: <b><%= ses.user_role %></b>. A page is not a back door: it reads and writes
with the rights of whoever asked for it, through the same xdb_acl as MQTT, MCP and
the telnet shell (docs/06_Access_and_Safety.md).</p>
<%@ include file="part/foot.ayp" %>
